{{Short description|Don't use an LLM to write an ANI report}}
{{essay|WP:LLMANI}}


==What is the LLM-written ANI report?==
Administrators and other regulars at [[WP:ANI]] have become familiar with a recurring pattern of complaints. It looks like this (and may have emojis starting each point which may/may not actually apply to the issue):

{{blockquote|I am requesting administrative review of [editor] due to their pattern of X, Y and Z at [topic area]. Here is another sentence briefly giving context about the dispute. Maybe there's a third sentence.

===1. The first complaint===
"Quoted text from an edit"

*This source does not say Thing A. There is no source supporting this. [[WP:V]], [[WP:OR]]

===2. The second complaint===
According to [[WP:POLICY]], editors should never Thing B. [[WP:GUIDELINE]] says that article content should not Thing D. On Wikipedia, [wishful conjecture that does not follow from the prior two statements].

This is a serious violation of [[WP:BLP]]

===3. The third complaint===
*Possible hounding across multiple articles [[WP:HOUND]]
*Reverts edits and tells people to discuss on the talk page without engaging in discussion [[WP:DISCUSS]]

===The complaint without the number===
On articles such as [subject1] and [subject2], [editor] has:
* Removed sources relating to X [[WP:V]]
* Misrepresented coverage of Y [[WP:DUE]]
* Received a contentious topic notice, which definitely displays a problem with their editing in itself [[WP:CTOP]]

===5. We remembered the number again===
During my discussion with [editor], another user [well-known admin] collapsed my text and said I was using an LLM. This made it difficult to continue discussion. [Well-known admin] contributed to a hostile environment. [[WP:AGF]], [[WP:CIVIL]]

===Requested action===
I am requesting administrative review of [editor] and [well-known admin]'s behavior to establish:
*whether this constitutes disruptive behavior or tendentious editing
*whether to issue a topic ban or warning
*how to ensure that editors can contribute constructively going forward
<small>–Preceding [[Wikipedia:Signatures|unsigned]] comment added by ''OPUSERNAME''</small>
}}

There's small variations. Sometimes there will be more [[WP:LLMSIGNS]] like stray markup or incorrect line breaks. Sometimes the signature will be included. The exact content and number of sections can vary. Sometimes there will be diffs, sometimes there won't (likely a function of how savvy the user is to insist that the LLM use provided diffs in its writeup). The tone will always be crisply professional and authoritative, even when the cited policies and guidelines are not. The reports look like [[Wikipedia:Administrators'_noticeboard/IncidentArchive1208#Conduct_concern_regarding_User:TarnishedPath_on_Talk:Daniel_Andrews|this]] and [[Wikipedia:Administrators'_noticeboard/IncidentArchive1207#User:Deamonpen_–_repeated_BLP/source_problems_on_Peter_Thiel–related_topics|this]] and [[Wikipedia:Administrators'_noticeboard/IncidentArchive1213#Infobox_ordering_and_captioning_for_Lion_and_Sun_designs|this]] and [[Special:Diff/1339069182|this]]. It's not clear whether it's one LLM in particular that produces requests like this, or a subset of them, or all of them, nor is it clear where the LLMs got the idea that this is what an ANI report looks like. It's not. Normal ANI reports look like [[Wikipedia:Administrators'_noticeboard/IncidentArchive1207#Personal_attack|this]] and [[Wikipedia:Administrators'_noticeboard/IncidentArchive1207#WP:CT/CASTE_based_disruption|this]] and [[Wikipedia:Administrators'_noticeboard/IncidentArchive1207#Removal_of_another_editor's_edit_in_a_discussion|this]] and [[Wikipedia:Administrators'_noticeboard/IncidentArchive1207#Temp_account_sockpuppeting_to_repeatedly_reinsert_BLPVIO_content_against_consensus,_refusal_to_DROPTHESTICK|this]].{{ref|a}}

==Why these reports are a problem==
All of the [[WP:LLMTALK|general considerations]] regarding LLM use in discussions on Wikipedia apply to ANI. But beyond that, in producing these reports, LLMs are throwing together dozens of superficially plausible allegations at once, which requires a lot of effort for the community and the accused editor to respond to. While some attempts to use LLMs at ANI are sincere, it is also very easy to turn these tools into a vector for harassment and abuse. It is not fair or reasonable to ask editors who volunteer their time on Wikipedia to put up with the prospect of such harassment. If you have a genuine concern about someone else's activity on Wikipedia, follow the rules and draft a complaint yourself. If you need help, ask other editors, not the AI.

